.\" $NetBSD$
.Dd June 20, 2026
.Dt FREE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm free
.Nd display the amount of free and used physical memory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl b | Fl k | Fl m | Fl g | Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
displays the total amount of physical memory in the system together with
the amount currently used, free, and held in the file-system buffer cache.
The values are obtained from the
.Va vm.uvmexp2
.Xr sysctl 7
node.
.Pp
By default sizes are shown in kibibytes.
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b
Show sizes in bytes.
.It Fl k
Show sizes in kibibytes (the default).
.It Fl m
Show sizes in mebibytes.
.It Fl g
Show sizes in gibibytes.
.It Fl h
Show sizes in a human-readable form, choosing the largest unit that
keeps the value below 1024.
.El
.Pp
The
.Dq used
column is computed as
.Dq total
minus
.Dq free ;
the
.Dq cached
column counts pages held for the file-system cache, which the system can
reclaim under memory pressure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr top 1 ,
.Xr sysctl 7
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
command was written for
.Nx Ns -based
MINIX 3.
